@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #F7F9FC
skinparam StateBorderColor #4A6FA5
title E03: running and restart_blocked (one transition per tick)

state "Stopped\nrunning=false\nrestart_blocked=false" as Stopped
state "Running\nrunning=true" as Running
state "RestartBlocked\nrunning=false\nrestart_blocked=true" as Blocked

[*] --> Stopped
Stopped --> Running : START pressed, STOP released\n(both healthy)
Running --> Stopped : STOP pressed (healthy),\nno restart block
Stopped --> Blocked : START or STOP fault
Running --> Blocked : STOP fault, or stopped\nwhile restart block is set
Blocked --> Stopped : both healthy and\nSTART released
Blocked --> Blocked : START still held,\nor any fault

note right of Running
  A START fault while running keeps
  running (STOP healthy and released)
  but sets restart_blocked. It clears
  when START is seen released
  while both inputs are healthy.
end note
@enduml
